Minimal curve: y^2+y=x^3-1; discriminant=-243; P=(1,0).
Hessian determinant: 24*x*(y - z)*(y + 2*z)
On the affine curve: Hessian=24*x*(x^3-3).
Three-division polynomial: 3*x*(x**3 - 3)
Flex residue fields: Q at O; Q(zeta_3) at x=0;
  Q(cuberoot(3)) at y=1 and y=-2 (two separate degree-three orbits).
All finite flex tangents meet the cubic with multiplicity exactly three.
Normalized units (leading coefficient +1 at O, parameter -x/y):
  w - y ; value at P = w ; field norm = 1
  a**2*x - y - 2 ; value at P = a**2 - 2 ; field norm = 1
  -a**2*x - y + 1 ; value at P = 1 - a**2 ; field norm = -8
Each normalized unit has divisor 3(d-O).
Hence its square-root cover is geometrically connected, branched at d,O, genus2.
Primary-component reductions verified in 857 cyclic test cases.
All exact rank-one unit checks passed.
